 "method": {
  "lab": "Brand sRGB -> CIELAB D50 (Bradford), the ICC convention Pantone's D50 Lab uses.",
  "pantone_ranking": "CIEDE2000 (kit.de2000), median over the value sets available for each colour: pcm = Pantone Color Manager V4 Lab, plus = PANTONE+ Lab (or ok2pan Lab where PANTONE+ lacks the colour), web = Pantone's published sRGB (Solid Coated, only where the ink is inside sRGB).",
  "cmyk": "Pillow ImageCms (littleCMS), sRGB -> profile, relative colorimetric + black point compensation. raw = 8-bit result in %, clean = whole %, 1-2 % traces dropped and 98-99 % made solid when that costs <= 0.5 dE. rt_de2000 = back to Lab with the same intent + BPC (gamut loss); paper_relative_de2000 = back to Lab without BPC (what the sheet measures against its white)."
 },
 "document_profile": {
  "recommended": "Coated GRACoL 2006 (ISO 12647-2:2004)",
  "file": "CoatedGRACoL2006.icc",
  "why": "Darker black point and higher ink limit (TAC 329 against 295 on SWOP v2): the navy prints at paper-relative dE 5.5 on GRACoL 2006 against 8.6 on SWOP v2, the blue matches as well, and GRACoL 2006 / FOGRA39 are the ISO 12647-2 coated-sheetfed conditions most brand collateral is printed to, while SWOP v2 is a web-offset publication condition. SWOP v2 is better only for Ribbon Cyan (dE 4.2 against 5.5). Coated FOGRA39 is the equivalent choice for vendors who print to ISO 12647-2 / FOGRA39 (common outside North America); builds for all three are given. Ask each vendor for its printing condition first."
 },
